      "text": "To find the area of the parallelogram generated by the vectors \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\), we need to calculate the magnitude of the cross product of these two vectors. The cross product of two vectors \\(\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} a_1 \\\\ a_2 \\\\ a_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} b_1 \\\\ b_2 \\\\ b_3 \\end{pmatrix}\\) in \\(\\mathbb{R}^3\\) is given by:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ a_1 & a_2 & a_3 \\\\ b_1 & b_2 & b_3 \\end{vmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} a_2 b_3 - a_3 b_2 \\\\ a_3 b_1 - a_1 b_3 \\\\ a_1 b_2 - a_2 b_1 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nFor the vectors \\(\\mathbf{a} = \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}\\) and \\(\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}\\), the cross product is:\n\n\\[\n\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b} = \\begin{pmatrix} (1)(4) - (-2)(-3) \\\\ (-2)(1) - (3)(4) \\\\ (3)(-3) - (1)(1) \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 - 6 \\\\ -2 - 12 \\\\ -9 - 1 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}\n\\]\n\nThe magnitude of the cross product vector \\(\\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ -10 \\end{pmatrix}\\) is:\n\n\\[\n\\|\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{b}\\| = \\sqrt{(-2)^2 + (-14)^2 + (-10)^2} = \\sqrt{4 + 196 + 100} = \\sqrt{300} = 10\\sqrt{3}\n\\]\n\nThus, the area of the parallelogram is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{10\\sqrt{3}}\n\\]",
