      "text": "Let $A$ and $B$ be the points represented by $\\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}$ and $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix}$, respectively. The area of the parallelogram generated by $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ is found by taking the absolute value of the determinant of a matrix whose columns are $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ and $\\overrightarrow{AD}$, where $D$ is the origin. In this case, $\\overrightarrow{BD}$ is $\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 4 \\end{pmatrix} - \\begin{pmatrix} 3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 6 \\end{pmatrix}$. The matrix giving the sides of the parallelogram is\n\\[\\begin{pmatrix} 3 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]The determinant of this matrix is $3(-3) - 1(1) = -10$, so the area is $\\boxed{10}.$. The answer is 10",
